  "description": "Removal of existing phone box. Installation of 1No. BT Street Hub Unit and associated illuminated digital advertisement panels on either side of the unit. (Associated Advertisement Consent application ref.2026/0187)",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed Street Hub, by reason of its scale, design and location would fail to minimise street clutter, result in loss of public open space and harm to the character and appearance of the local area.Whilst the proposal would result in some facilities for the general public, these benefits are low and do not outweigh the harm identified. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies D3, D8 of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1, LP9, and LP22 of the Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
